<title>SINGAPORE: U.S., EU closer to infotech accord - Barshefsky.</title>
<headline>U.S., EU closer to infotech accord - Barshefsky.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States and the European Union made progress on Tuesday in resolving their differences over an accord to eliminate tariffs on a wide range of information technology, Acting U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky told reporters.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have made progress,&quot; Barshefsky said ahead of a meeting of the Big Four major trade powers -- the United States, the EU, Japan and Canada.</p>
<p>EU Trade Commissioner Sir Leon Brittan also told reporters that talks between him and Barshefsky on the sidelines of the World Trade Organisation ministerial conference in Singapore had gone well.</p>
<p>Asked whether an agreement was at hand, Brittan said: &quot;Not yet, but we are making good progress.&quot;</p>
</text>
